# calculate_molecular_fraction_BR06 called directly (R/src/model_h2_chemistry.c:117-125): the stellar scale height (:48-60) and the pressure-based fraction (:68-101).
# The fused height (H:56): SAGE26's object fuses -0.23 + 0.8 * log10(R*) into one fmadd
# (model_h2_chemistry.o 0x50). An exhaustive scan of every positive finite float R* finds
# exactly one, 0x338656be (6.25563956e-08 pc), at which the fused and unfused doubles narrow
# to different float log_h_star (-0x1.7f8d06p+2 fused, -0x1.7f8d08p+2 unfused); with this gas
# and stellar density the return separates: 0x38e862a8 fused, 0x38e862b0 unfused.
# On R2 the public routine itself is not called (only the single-slab branch, S:235, and other prescriptions call it); its core is what the radial integration calls per annulus.
# Constructed input (not R2 output); every value is set explicitly.
# Reachability: constructed routine-domain probe (the only float scale length that separates).
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
routine calculate_molecular_fraction_BR06

f32 call.gas_surface_density_msun_pc2 0x358637bd  # 9.99999997e-07  (Msun/pc^2)
f32 call.stellar_surface_density_msun_pc2 0x3f800000  # 1  (Msun/pc^2)
f32 call.disk_scale_length_pc 0x338656be  # 6.25563956e-08  (pc)
